Linux/gcc build fixes for the published OrcaRouter fork revision
(igorls/ninfer @ 91ce2f2c).

The revision's only qualified toolchain is MSVC + CUDA 13.3; three constructs
in its qwen3_8_flash_next (Flash-Next) target do not build under Linux/gcc:
its sources use std::max over an initializer_list without <algorithm>, alignas
on an `extern __shared__` declaration, and checked_add/checked_mul calls that
deduce T from both arguments (only valid where size_t is unsigned long long).

The variant builds with CUDA 13.3.1 for a separate reason: the same target
includes <cub/device/device_topk.cuh>, which only exists in CCCL as shipped
with CUDA 13.3 (13.1 has no such header at all).

